    "C52","C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "All L1 gold records report oral bioavailability values or qualitative extents above the F>=20% threshold, with numeric values from about 45% to about 108% and qualitative reports of complete or very good absorption; no L1 record reports F<20%.",
      "card_ids": [
        "C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C12","C13","C14","C15","C16","C17","C18","C19","C20","C21","C22","C23","C24","C25","C26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records are predominantly consistent with the high-F direction, including ethinylestradiol 76.9%, pengitoxin 77.9-87.2%, beta-methyldigoxin 0.87-0.92, CDCA 108%, digitoxin 89.7%, and UDCA formulation enhancements; the qualitative note that CDCA is 'not highly systemically available' (C31) is not threshold-relevant and is outweighed by quantitative L1 records for the same context.",
      "card_ids": ["C27","C28","C29","C30","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption and permeability records for steroid-like molecules show high fraction absorbed (hydrocortisone 89-95% and fa=0.90; prednisolone 95%; corticosterone complete), high permeability (megestrol acetate BCS class II), and complete absorption of danazol solution in dogs; these support the absorption component for a lipophilic steroid query.",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C54","C55","C56","C58","C59","C60","C62","C63"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 dissolution records in PEG 6000 dispersions are formulation-specific and show fast dissolution when formulated; they do not provide affirmative evidence of F<20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C53","C57","C61"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No supplied record provides affirmative threshold-relevant evidence of F<20% for the query; the unfavorable solubility prior is estimated from logP/ionization rather than measured, and the F>=20% threshold may be met with high permeability even if solubility is limited.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C52","C59","C62"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral versus intravenous bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific dose, formulation, species, or condition data.",
    "L4 records are for other steroid molecules and some are formulation-specific; transfer to the query is indirect.",
    "Query aqueous solubility and dissolution are not experimentally measured; high logP suggests a limitation but does not establish F<20%.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance of the query are not experimentally characterized.",
    "Gut-wall efflux and intestinal metabolism evidence (L5) has not yet been provided."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F>=20%) because all transferable L1 gold records are above threshold, L2 is predominantly supportive, and L4 intestinal absorption/permeability records for steroid-like molecules support high absorption; no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence indicates F<20%. Confidence remains moderate due to lack of direct query-specific F data and unmeasured solubility/first-pass."
}

